# Pytest markers (required)

Every test function **must** be tagged `@pytest.mark.unit` or `@pytest.mark.integration`. Root [`conftest.py`](conftest.py) fails collection if either is missing. Markers are registered in [`pytest.ini`](pytest.ini).

## Definitions

| Marker | Use when |
|--------|----------|
| `unit` | In-process only: `services.py`, models, form `clean_*`, helpers. No Django test client, no `call_command`, no HTTP. |
| `integration` | Django test client (`client.get` / `client.post`), management commands (`call_command`), WeasyPrint/PDF or quote HTTP. |

`@pytest.mark.django_db` is separate — add it when the test touches the database (most tests here). A test can be `unit` + `django_db`, or `integration` + `django_db`.

Pure helpers with no DB (e.g. `normalize_lang`) get `unit` only.

## How to tag

**Uniform file** — module-level:

```python
pytestmark = [pytest.mark.unit, pytest.mark.django_db]
```

**Mixed file** — per test:

```python
@pytest.mark.integration
@pytest.mark.django_db
def test_staff_can_create_client(client, staff_user):
    ...
```

When adding tests, tag them in the same PR — do not leave unmarked tests for a later pass.

## Commands

```bash
pytest -m unit
pytest -m integration
pytest
```

## Checklist for new/changed tests

- [ ] Exactly one of `unit` or `integration` on every `test_*`
- [ ] `django_db` present when the test needs the DB (or uses `db` / ORM fixtures)
- [ ] `pytest -q` green after changes
